         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Matching the Tables of 2, 4 and 8\n\nEight is the meeting point of the tables of 2 and of 4:\n\n2 × 2 × 2 × N = 4 × 2 × N = 8 × N\n\nMultiplying by 8 means multiplying by 2 three times in a row (8 × N = 2 × 2 × 2 × N), and it is also the same as doubling a result of the table of 4 (8 × N = 4 × 2 × N).\n\nTap an equality on the left, then its result on the right. Each result shows groups of eight characters, so you can count them to check.\n\n- Levels 1 and 2: 2 × 2 × 2 × N = 8 × N.\n- Levels 3 and 4: 4 × 2 × N = 8 × N.\n\nMatch every pair to finish a level.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
